Subject: [PATCH 040/230] Claim the anchor on the first club pick so a
 same-tick second pick cannot re-anchor
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two onboarding club tiles tapped in the same tick both saw the favorite count
as 0 and both ran the follow-then-anchor flow, so two anchor PUTs fired and the
last one won — the anchor landed on the second club, not the first. A
synchronous first-pick coordinator now claims the anchor for the earliest pick;
any pick arriving while it is in flight is only followed, and the claim is
released on settle so a real retry can still anchor. A same-tick test pins one
anchor request, on the first-picked club, with both clubs followed.

